URL:https://mae.princeton.edu/events/2026/nuclear-electric-propulsion-progr
 ess-challenges-and-path-high-power-space-systems
LOCATION:Bowen Hall
SUMMARY:Nuclear Electric Propulsion: Progress\, Challenges\, and the Path t
 o High-Power Space Systems
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Abstract:Nuclear electric propulsion (NEP) offers the potential
  to fundamentally expand the capability and reach of spacecraft\, but real
 izing that potential requires overcoming significant challenges in reactor
  technology\, power conversion and distribution\, thermal management\, ele
 ctric propulsion\, and system integration. This seminar will examine the c
 urrent state of NEP development\, highlighting recent progress while explo
 ring the demanding requirements associated with operating high-power syste
 ms continuously for years or even decades in the space environment.
CATEGORIES:MAE Departmental Seminars
DTSTAMP:20260824T163808Z
